     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Volume",
     "md": "**Volume** is the amount of space a solid takes up. We measure it in **cubic units**: cm³ and m³. A cube of side 1 cm has a volume of 1 cm³. For a **cuboid**: volume = length × width × height. For a **cube** of side $s$: volume = $s \\times s \\times s$."
